-- title:
--   Units of a conjugated Eichler order count automorphisms preserving kerψ
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of prime characteristic $q'$ that is algebraic over $\mathbb{Z}/q'$, and let $X_1$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ all of whose points killed by $q'$ are zero. Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ satisfy `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`: $a<0$, $b<0$, and for each height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ the algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $q'\in v$. Let $\Lambda_1\subseteq\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be a maximal order (an order maximal among the orders containing it) and $\theta_1$ an injective ring homomorphism from the subring `rationalEndSubring` of $\operatorname{End}(X_1(\kappa))$ generated by the rationally represented endomorphisms (together with $0$) onto $\Lambda_1$. Let $M'\neq 0$ be a natural number not divisible by $q'$, and $m'$ a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\widehat{\mathbb{Q}}$ (finite adeles) with $m'$ lying in the adelic box [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) $\Lambda_1$ generated by the elements $z\otimes\alpha$, $z\in\Lambda_1$, $\alpha$ an integral adele, with $M'\cdot (m')^{-1}$ also in that box, and with $\Lambda_1$ conjugated by $m'$ again a maximal order. Put $S=\Lambda_1\cap m'\Lambda_1 m'^{-1}$ (the intersection of $\Lambda_1$ with [`Submodule.conjByFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L31) $\Lambda_1\,m'$), assumed of relative index $M'$ in $\Lambda_1$ as additive groups. Let $x$ be a further adelic unit, $W$ an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$, $\chi: X_1\to W$ a nonzero additive map in `rationalHomSet`, and $d$ a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ such that $\theta_1$ carries the set of endomorphisms of $X_1$ of the form $\rho\circ\chi$ with $\rho\in$ `rationalHomSet` $(W,X_1)$ onto the quaternion conjugate (`star`) of $d\cdot(\mathbb{H}\cap x\Lambda_1)$, i.e. of $d\cdot$ [`Submodule.ofFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L19) $\Lambda_1\,x$. Let $W'$ be elliptic, $\psi: W\to W'$ and $\psi': W'\to W$ in `rationalHomSet` with $\psi'\circ\psi$ and $\psi\circ\psi'$ both multiplication by $M'$, and assume likewise that $\theta_1$ carries the set of endomorphisms $\rho\circ(\psi\circ\chi)$ of $X_1$, $\rho\in$ `rationalHomSet` $(W',X_1)$, onto the conjugate of $d\cdot$ [`Submodule.ofFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L19) $\Lambda_1\,(x m')$. Then the number of $u\in\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ lying in $x S x^{-1}$ (the module [`Submodule.conjByFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L31) $S\,x$) and admitting a two-sided inverse inside that module equals the number of additive endomorphisms $\iota$ of $W(\kappa)$ that lie in `rationalHomSet` $(W,W)$, admit a two-sided compositional inverse in `rationalHomSet` $(W,W)$, and satisfy $\iota(\ker\psi)=\ker\psi$.
--
--   This is the quaternionic half of a Deuring-type dictionary: through the transport $\rho\mapsto d^{-1}\overline{\theta_1(\rho\chi)}$ the rational endomorphisms of $W$ correspond to $\mathbb{H}\cap x\Lambda_1 x^{-1}$ and those preserving $\ker\psi$ to the conjugated Eichler order $\mathbb{H}\cap xSx^{-1}$, so that its unit group is counted by the automorphisms of $W$ fixing $\ker\psi$. It feeds the comparison of place widths with class weights on the Čerednik–Drinfeld side, where the counts of automorphisms of enhanced supersingular curves are matched with unit counts in Eichler orders.
